    "title": "World Baseball Classic scores: Updated results, standings for every 2026 WBC game | Sporting News",
    "text": "If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation. Learn more > It's a World Baseball Classic year — meaning baseball fans will get two weeks full of competitive action, featuring some of the sport's biggest stars, in the month of March prior to MLB's Opening Day.Pool play officially opens on March 4, with 20 international teams eyeing a tournament title. The top-two finishers from each of the five-team pools will advance to the quarterfinals for a single-elimination bracket.WATCH: Stream the 2026 World Baseball Classic live through Fubo (free trial)Japan is the defending WBC champion, having taken down the United States in the 2023 Finals, but a star-studded American team enters as the 2026 favorite — while the Dominican Republic, Japan and Venezuela represent a few more top contenders.Here's a look at the full 2026 World Baseball Classic schedule, along with the bracket and updated results throughout the tournament.WORLD BASEBALL CLASSIC HQ: Live scores | Updated standings | Full TV scheduleWorld Baseball Classic daily schedule and scoresThe World Baseball Classic will feature games nearly every day for two weeks.All times listed are Eastern Time.MORE WORLD BASEBALL CLASSIC 2026: Sporting News' expert predictions for World Baseball ClassicFull list of players for 20 World Baseball Classic teamsBest MLB players in WBC, from Aaron Judge to Geraldo Perdomo8 best games to watch on WBC scheduleRanking the World Baseball Classic teams from best to worstWednesday, March 4MatchupTime (ET)PoolAustralia 3, Chinese Taipei 0FINALCThursday, March 5MatchupTime (ET)PoolKorea 11, Czechia 4FINALCAustralia 5, Czechia 1FINALCFriday, March 6MatchupTime (ET)PoolJapan 13, Chinese Taipei 0FINALCCuba 3, Panama 1FINALAVenezuela 6, Netherlands 2FINALDMexico 8, Great Britain 2FINALBPuerto Rico 5, Colombia 0FINALADominican Republic 12, Nicaragua 3FINALDUnited States 15, Brazil 5FINALBChinese Taipei 14, Czechia 